ent-ComputerTurretCommandTSF = TSF turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for TSF turrets on an outpost. Officers and above can open it.
    .suffix = Outpost
ent-ComputerTurretCommandEmpire = imperial turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for imperial turrets on an outpost. Officers and above can open it.
    .suffix = Outpost
ent-ComputerTurretCommandNT = NanoTrasen turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for NanoTrasen turrets on an outpost. The station representative can open it.
    .suffix = Outpost
ent-ComputerTurretCommandUSSP = USSP turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for USSP turrets on an outpost. Sergeants and the commissar can open it.
    .suffix = Outpost
ent-ComputerTurretCommandRenegate = renegade turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for renegade turrets on an outpost. Officers and above can open it.
    .suffix = Outpost
ent-ComputerTurretCommandPDV = PDV turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for PDV turrets on an outpost. Command staff can open it.
    .suffix = Outpost
ent-ComputerTurretCommandVG = Viper Group turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for Viper Group turrets on an outpost. Lieutenants and the commander can open it.
    .suffix = Outpost
ent-ComputerTurretCommandTSFShuttle = TSF shuttle turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for TSF turrets on this shuttle. Any TSF member can open it, including a recruit.
    .suffix = Shuttle
ent-ComputerTurretCommandEmpireShuttle = imperial shuttle turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for imperial turrets on this shuttle. Any imperial can open it, including a neophyte.
    .suffix = Shuttle
ent-ComputerTurretCommandNTShuttle = NanoTrasen shuttle turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for NanoTrasen turrets on this shuttle. Any NanoTrasen crew member can open it.
    .suffix = Shuttle
ent-ComputerTurretCommandUSSPShuttle = USSP shuttle turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for USSP turrets on this shuttle. Any USSP member can open it, including a rifleman.
    .suffix = Shuttle
ent-ComputerTurretCommandRenegateShuttle = renegade shuttle turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for renegade turrets on this shuttle. Any renegade can open it, including a flunky.
    .suffix = Shuttle
ent-ComputerTurretCommandPDVShuttle = PDV shuttle turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for PDV turrets on this shuttle. Any PDV member can open it.
    .suffix = Shuttle
ent-ComputerTurretCommandVGShuttle = Viper Group shuttle turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for Viper Group turrets on this shuttle. Any Viper Group member can open it, including an infanteer.
    .suffix = Shuttle
ent-ComputerTurretCommandShip = ship turret command console
    .desc = Doctrine and friend or foe lists for mercenary and adventurer turrets on this ship. Opens only for the ship owner, the same lock as the helm and gunnery console.
ent-WeaponTurretMercenary = mercenary ballistic turret
    .desc = A mercenary ship turret. It obeys this ship's turret command console.
ent-WeaponTurretMercenaryPacked = packed mercenary turret
    .desc = A disassembled mercenary ballistic turret. Deploy it on the deck.
ent-WeaponTurretAdventurer = adventurer ballistic turret
    .desc = An adventurer ship turret. It obeys this ship's turret command console.
ent-WeaponTurretAdventurerPacked = packed adventurer turret
    .desc = A disassembled adventurer ballistic turret. Deploy it on the deck.
ent-MagazineTurretBallistic = ballistic turret cartridge kit
    .desc = Sixty rounds of 7.62x39mm. Accepts any round of that caliber. Load it into a ballistic command turret, or the turret cannot fire.
ent-MagazineTurretShotgun = shotgun turret cartridge kit
    .desc = Sixteen shells of 12 gauge. Accepts any 12-gauge shell. Load it into a shotgun command turret, or the turret cannot fire.
ent-MagazineTurretSniper = sniper turret cartridge kit
    .desc = Eight rounds of 12.7x99mm. Accepts any round of that caliber. Load it into a sniper command turret, or the turret cannot fire.
ent-MagazineTurretMachinegun = machine gun turret cartridge kit
    .desc = One hundred and twenty rounds of 7.62x39mm. Accepts any round of that caliber. Load it into a machine-gun command turret, or the turret cannot fire.
ent-MagazineTurretBallisticEmpty = empty ballistic turret cartridge kit
    .desc = An empty box for sixty rounds of any 7.62x39mm. Fill it, then load it into a ballistic command turret.
ent-MagazineTurretShotgunEmpty = empty shotgun turret cartridge kit
    .desc = An empty box for sixteen shells of any 12 gauge. Fill it, then load it into a shotgun command turret.
ent-MagazineTurretSniperEmpty = empty sniper turret cartridge kit
    .desc = An empty box for eight rounds of any 12.7x99mm. Fill it, then load it into a sniper command turret.
ent-MagazineTurretMachinegunEmpty = empty machine gun turret cartridge kit
    .desc = An empty box for one hundred and twenty rounds of any 7.62x39mm. Fill it, then load it into a machine-gun command turret.
ent-TurretCommandShipCircuitboard = ship turret command console board
    .desc = A computer board for a ship turret command console. Outsiders cannot open it: it uses the same lock as the helm.

